 rest_capacity:   remaining vehicle capacity\n        demands:         demand of every node (index 0 = depot demand = 0)\n        distance_matrix: pairwise Euclidean distance matrix\n    Returns:\n        Index of the next node to visit, or 0 to return to the depot early.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_node = int(current_node)\n    depot = int(depot)\n    unvisited_nodes = np.asarray(unvisited_nodes, dtype=int)\n    demand = demands[unvisited_nodes].astype(float)\n\n    d_cur = distance_matrix[current_node][unvisited_nodes].astype(float)\n    d_depot = distance_matrix[depot][unvisited_nodes].astype(float)\n    d_depot_cur = float(distance_matrix[depot][current_node])\n\n    cap = float(rest_capacity)\n    fill = demand / cap if cap > 0.0 else np.zeros_like(demand)\n\n    # Radial progress: how much closer to the depot this move brings us.\n    # Positive means we move inward (toward depot), which we want to defer.\n    inward = np.maximum(d_depot_cur - d_depot, 0.0)\n\n    # Base: prefer nearby customers.\n    base = d_cur\n\n    # Lock in far-from-depot customers early (big depot distance is costly to\n    # leave for later when capacity is tight).\n    far_reward = d_depot\n\n    # Prefer customers that use up a good chunk of remaining capacity.\n    fill_reward = fill\n\n    score = base - 0.35 * far_reward - 0.6 * fill_reward * d_cur + 0.5 * inward\n\n    return int(unvisited_nodes[np.argmin(score)])","code_sha256":"3b89c3ba7ef55b26446faa9733437f259263566c3183a0b516c0a8c64d4d00c8","elapsed_seconds":0.25,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"f3aae49f41bd480cb1e63d4eb18c3169","generation_parents":[{"algorithm":"Score each feasible customer by a polar-coordinate \"savings potential\": the detour it induces versus the direct depot leg (d_cur + d_depot_to_customer - d_depot_to_current), normalized by its demand share, then break ties toward customers forming the tightest angular sector with the current node to build coherent radial routes.","code_sha256":"